Template: ai-sandbox-server/onboard
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Run the ai-sandbox onboarding wizard now?
 The wizard captures the SSH key, git author identity, and an optional
 GitHub token so newly spawned sessions can clone and commit out of the box.
 .
 You can always (re-)run it later with: sudo aisandboxctl onboard
 Choose no to defer onboarding entirely.

Template: ai-sandbox-server/git-name
Type: string
Description: Git author name for commits made inside sessions:
 Seeds /etc/ai-sandbox-server/secrets/gitconfig. Both the name and the email
 are required to onboard during install; leave either blank to defer
 onboarding and configure it later with `sudo aisandboxctl onboard`.

Template: ai-sandbox-server/git-email
Type: string
Description: Git author email for commits made inside sessions:
 Seeds /etc/ai-sandbox-server/secrets/gitconfig alongside the author name.

Template: ai-sandbox-server/ssh-key-path
Type: string
Description: Path to the SSH private key for git over SSH (optional):
 Copied (passphrase-stripped) to /etc/ai-sandbox-server/secrets/git-key so
 sessions can clone/push over SSH. Leave blank to add the key later with
 `sudo aisandboxctl onboard --git-key <path>`.

Template: ai-sandbox-server/gh-token
Type: password
Description: GitHub personal access token (optional):
 Stored at /etc/ai-sandbox-server/secrets/gh-token for `gh` API calls. Leave
 blank to skip; git clone/push still works over SSH without it. The value is
 cleared from the debconf database immediately after install.

Template: ai-sandbox-server/claude-preinit-note
Type: note
Description: Claude pre-init: interactive login now, or a headless seed later
 The Claude OAuth login needs an interactive terminal and a built container
 image. When you install from a terminal, the post-install step offers to run
 the full wizard now — including this login and the image build — so spawned
 sessions start past Claude's first-run setup. When no terminal is available
 it is skipped and the install completes with one next step: capture it later
 with `sudo aisandboxctl onboard` from a terminal, or seed it unattended with
 `sudo aisandboxctl onboard --claude-config-source <dir>`.
